# local instance config (references real paths/names — not part of the shareable package)
config/codemap.toml

# destination-only stamps, written by deploy.sh INTO a vendored copy and never present in the
# canonical pack (docs/packaging-contract.md criterion 23). Ignored rather than merely "not added":
# both were found TRACKED in this repo on 2026-09-15, having arrived with a deployment that was
# moved in to become the canonical tree, where they asserted canonical_repo=unknown, a tracked_ref
# naming a tag this repo does not have, and an absolute host path in pack_path. An ignore entry is
# what stops `git add -A` sweeping them back in. tests/test_packaging.py::test_c23 enforces both
# halves (ignored here, and absent from the index).
/PROVENANCE
/PACK_SOURCE

# pending commit-message files prepared by a sandbox session for the owner to commit from
# (`git commit -F <file>`); each change gets its own name so two pending messages cannot be
# confused. Transient working state, never pack content — and ignoring them keeps the same
# `git add -A` that committed the stamps above from committing a commit message too.
/COMMIT_MSG-*.txt
.venv/
.install-lock
*.candidates.json
.harness-memory/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
